      "severity": "info",
      "text": "spark serve --check-kernels is a real preflight and worth running first: it loads the model, resolves every kernel lookup and exits with the number that did not resolve. Here it reported 251 lookups, 0 unresolved, 1 expected-absent for (qwen3.8-27b, sm_121, nvfp4), kernel_set_hash 7d4320ea200f. An unresolved lookup does not error at serve time - it silently takes a slower dispatch path."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Four of this configuration's knobs have no CLI flag and are read from the environment (ATLAS_PREFILL_CODISPATCH, ATLAS_FP8_ROWWISE, ATLAS_MTP_DCUT_RATIO, ATLAS_MTP_K_LADDER). The published recipe says the ladder does not reproduce without them, so they are registered as engine params and passed in args; a fingerprint that dropped them would merge two configurations that differ by more than 20% at C=2."
    },
    {
